=== QT024 | sorted attribute on a literal out of order
r:`s#3 1 2

=== QT024 | symbols sort by byte, so a lowercase before an uppercase is out of order
r:`s#`a`B

=== QT024 | unique attribute on a repeated item
r:`u#1 1 2

=== QT024 | parted attribute on a value that comes back
r:`p#1 2 1

=== clean | ties, a null first and contiguous runs are what the attributes allow
r1:`s#1 1 2
r2:`s#0N 1 2
r3:`p#1 1 2
r4:`s#`B`a

=== clean | grouped never fails, and a literal that runs on is not the operand
r1:`g#1 2 1
r2:`s#3 1 2,0

=== QE006 | a date that does not exist
r:2024.02.30

=== QE006 | 1900 was not a leap year
r:1900.02.29

=== QE006 | nor is there a thirteenth month
r:2024.13m

=== clean | 2000 was, and a path or a string with a bad date in it is not a literal
r1:2000.02.29
p:`:hdb/2024.02.30
s:"2024.02.30"

=== QE007 | select with no from
r:select a by b t

=== QE007 | inside a lambda too
f:{select x}

=== clean | a from anywhere before the statement ends, or the name assigned
r1:select from t
r2:update a:1 from t
.my.select:1

=== QT025 | signalling a number
f:{'1}

=== QT025 | a one-character string is a char atom, not a string
f:{'"x"}

=== clean | a string, a symbol, and the each adverb
f1:{'"xy"}
f2:{'`a}
f3:{x'1}
